ut wastes time when material is hanging.\n- N: b8-d7 – Develops knight but ignores free material.\n- B: d4-b2 – This move captures the white knight on b1, which is completely undefended. White has no way to recapture as the only nearby piece is the king on d1, too far away.\n\nThe knight on b1 is **hanging** — it is undefended and within capture range of the black bishop on d4. This is a free piece!\n\nReason: Capturing the undefended knight on b1 with the bishop (B: d4-b2) wins a full piece for no cost, dramatically increasing Black’s material advantage. This is the most forcing and highest-value move on the board. There are no immediate threats to the bishop after b2, and even if White plays Nb1 (but there is no knight left), it's irrelevant. This move also increases piece activity and central control.\n\nAnswer: B: d4-b2"}
