ng or rook, but risks weakening the kingside.\n- B: b2-a3 – Attacks c5 or potentially supports a future tactic, but less urgent.\n\nThe most promising move is B: b2-a1, which captures the undefended white knight on a1 (currently occupied by NWF1). This piece is completely unprotected, and capturing it gains significant material advantage without risk.\n\nReason: Winning a knight early in the game for free is a massive tempo and material gain. The bishop on b2 can legally move to a1 (diagonal path is clear after checking board state), and no white piece can recapture immediately. This move increases Black's winning probability substantially by increasing material advantage early.\n\nAnswer: B: b2-a1"}
