reatening anything concrete.\n\nBest Move: **Q: h1-f3**  \nThis move gives check to the white king at e2. The queen moves from h1 to f3, which is a diagonal attack. White will have limited escape options — the king can only go to d1, d2, or f1, all of which are heavily pressured. After Qf3+, Black can follow up with multiple mating threats, especially since the black bishop controls key light squares.\n\nReason: Delivering check with the queen maximizes pressure immediately. It limits White's responses and accelerates the path to checkmate. Among all valid moves, this is the most forcing and tactically dominant.\n\nAnswer: Q: h1-f3"}
